IMPORT prelude

-- Children and Young Persons Act 1993 (Singapore), Part 3 (Youth Court) -- arrest and release on a bond (s 36), constitution
-- (s 38), which court tries a child or young person (s 39), restrictions on imprisonment and corporal punishment (s 42), orders
-- on the parent (s 44), and the powers of the Youth Court on proof of an offence (s 49).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 July 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CYPA1993.txt, with the amendments of Act 30 of 2019, Act 31 of 2022 and Act 21 of 2025 in force
-- from 30 December 2025 shown in force. The section numbers are the BODY's: the powers on proof of an offence are s 49 (the
-- arrangement table at the top of the deposit is out of step and lists them against s 48).
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0266 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl, raised by the Jun Hao cradle-to-grave scenario
-- (event j023, 20 November 2021: a fifteen-year-old arrested for theft in a shop). The question: which court tries him, and what
-- orders may it make on proof of the offence instead of recording a conviction?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the general considerations (s 34); association with adult offenders (s 35); attendance of parents (s 37);
-- sittings and who may be present (s 40); removal of disqualification (s 41); grave crimes (s 43); remission from other courts
-- (s 45); the procedure in the Youth Court (s 47) except as a pointer; the presumption as to age (s 48); breach and variation
-- of s 49 orders (s 49(4) to (11)); juvenile case conferences (s 50); the content of the Second Schedule beyond a single flag;
-- the law in force before 30 December 2025, which governed the scenario's 2021 event and is not deposited.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Children and Young Persons Act 1993 -- the Youth Court`

§§ `36 -- arrest and release on a bond`

-- s 36(1): "Where a person apparently below 18 years of age is arrested ... and he or she is not released, he or she must be
-- brought before a Youth Court." (2): if that cannot be done immediately, the arresting officer must "without unnecessary delay
-- and within 48 hours after the person is arrested" take the person before a Magistrate.
-- (3): the court is to determine whether (a) the charge is triable only by the General Division of the High Court; (b) removal
-- from an undesirable person is necessary; (c) the person is likely to abscond; (d) may commit further offences; (e) evidence or
-- witnesses need protecting; (f) release would otherwise defeat the ends of justice. (4): "If none of the circumstances ...
-- exist, the Youth Court or Magistrate is to release the person on a bond". (5): the bond is entered into by the parent or
-- guardian or other person responsible.
GIVEN `apparent age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an arrested person not released must be brought before a Youth Court` IF
    `apparent age` LESS THAN 18

`the latest time in hours to bring the arrested person before a Magistrate` MEANS 48

DECLARE Section36Facts HAS
    `charge triable only by the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `undesirable association to break` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to abscond` IS A BOOLEAN
    `may commit further offences` IS A BOOLEAN
    `evidence or witnesses at risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `release would defeat the ends of justice` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A Section36Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrested person is to be released on a bond` IF
    NOT (   `the facts`'s `charge triable only by the High Court`
         OR `the facts`'s `undesirable association to break`
         OR `the facts`'s `likely to abscond`
         OR `the facts`'s `may commit further offences`
         OR `the facts`'s `evidence or witnesses at risk`
         OR `the facts`'s `release would defeat the ends of justice`)

§§ `38 -- constitution`

-- s 38(1): a judge of a Youth Court, "when determining the method of dealing with a child or young person in respect of whom a
-- written report is obtained", is "to sit with 2 advisers from a panel of advisers appointed by the President", except that where
-- the Court "cannot without adjournment be fully constituted" and an adjournment "would be inexpedient", the judge "may sit with
-- one adviser or ... alone". (3): otherwise the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 applies "as if that Court were a District Court".
-- The encoding returns the number of advisers REQUIRED: 2, or 0 where the exception applies (the judge may then sit with 1 or
-- none). Where no written report is obtained s 38(1) does not speak, and the encoding returns 0 (an inference from silence).
GIVEN `a written report was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN, `adjournment would be inexpedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the advisers the judge must sit with` MEANS
    IF `a written report was obtained` AND (NOT `adjournment would be inexpedient`) THEN 2 ELSE 0

§§ `39 -- which court tries the child or young person`

-- s 39(1): "no child or young person may be charged with or tried for any offence by a court of summary jurisdiction except a
-- Youth Court". (5): a Youth Court has jurisdiction to try all offences otherwise triable by a Magistrate's Court, a District
-- Court or the General Division of the High Court.
-- (2): an offence "triable only by the General Division of the High Court" must be tried there "unless (a) the Public Prosecutor
-- applies to the Youth Court to try such offence; and (b) the legal representative ... consents".
-- (2A): a young person "of 16 years of age or older but below 18" charged with an offence (a) "specified in the Second Schedule"
-- or (b) similar to one of which he or she was previously found guilty (after the 2022 amendment), "is to be tried ... by another
-- court of appropriate jurisdiction instead of a Youth Court" if (c) the Youth Court transmits the case on the Public
-- Prosecutor's fiat (2B), (2C), or (d) the Youth Court on its own motion so decides.
-- (3): a charge "made jointly against a child or young person and a person who has attained 18 years of age" is heard by a
-- court other than a Youth Court.
-- (6): "A person who has attained 18 years of age on the date of commencement of the hearing of the charge must not be tried for
-- any offence by a Youth Court." (7): a trial already under way may continue after the accused turns 18 (not encoded).
-- Not encoded: (2E), (2F) offences tried together; (4) another court discovering mid-hearing that the accused is a juvenile.
DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `the Youth Court`
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`

DECLARE Charge HAS
    `age at the start of the hearing` IS A NUMBER
    `triable only by the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Public Prosecutor applies for Youth Court trial` IS A BOOLEAN
    `legal representative consents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Second Schedule or repeat similar offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transmitted on fiat or by the court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `charged jointly with an adult` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the charge` IS A Charge
GIVETH A Court
`the court that tries the charge` MEANS
    IF `the charge`'s `age at the start of the hearing` AT LEAST 18 THEN `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`
    ELSE IF `the charge`'s `charged jointly with an adult` THEN `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`
         ELSE IF `the charge`'s `triable only by the High Court`
                 AND (NOT (`the charge`'s `Public Prosecutor applies for Youth Court trial` AND `the charge`'s `legal representative consents`))
              THEN `the General Division of the High Court`
              ELSE IF `the charge`'s `age at the start of the hearing` AT LEAST 16
                      AND `the charge`'s `Second Schedule or repeat similar offence`
                      AND `the charge`'s `transmitted on fiat or by the court's own motion`
                   THEN `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`
                   ELSE `the Youth Court`

§§ `42 -- restrictions on imprisonment and corporal punishment`

-- s 42(1): "A child must not be sentenced or ordered to be imprisoned for any offence". (2): a young person aged 14 or 15 must
-- not be imprisoned "unless the court certifies that he or she is of so unruly a character that he or she cannot be detained in a
-- place of detention or juvenile rehabilitation centre". (2A): a young person aged 16 or 17 likewise, unless (a) so certified, or
-- (b) to (e) convicted by the General Division of the High Court, or convicted by a court other than the Youth Court of (or
-- together with) a relevant offence mentioned in s 39(2A). The encoding folds (b) to (e) into one flag.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, `certified unruly` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted as in s 42(2A)(b) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 42 permits imprisonment` IF
    IF age LESS THAN 14 THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF age LESS THAN 16 THEN `certified unruly`
         ELSE IF age LESS THAN 18 THEN `certified unruly` OR `convicted as in s 42(2A)(b) to (e)`
              ELSE TRUE

-- s 42(3): "no child or young person of 14 years of age or older but below 16 years of age may be sentenced by any court other
-- than the General Division of the High Court to corporal punishment". (4): no young person of 16 or 17 may be, unless convicted
-- by the General Division of the High Court, or by a court other than the Youth Court of (or together with) a relevant offence
-- under s 39(2A). s 42 says nothing about corporal punishment of a person below 14; the encoding returns FALSE there as a
-- placeholder and asserts nothing (the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 was not read).
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, `convicted by the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted elsewhere of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 42 permits corporal punishment` IF
    IF age LESS THAN 14 THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF age LESS THAN 16 THEN `convicted by the High Court`
         ELSE IF age LESS THAN 18 THEN `convicted by the High Court` OR `convicted elsewhere of a relevant offence`
              ELSE TRUE

§§ `44 -- orders on the parent or guardian`

-- s 44(1): where a fine may be imposed and the Court thinks the case best met by a fine, damages or costs, it "must, if the
-- offender is a child or young person, order that the fine imposed and damages or costs awarded be paid by the parent or
-- guardian ... unless the Court is satisfied that the parent or guardian cannot be found or that the parent or guardian has not
-- conduced to the commission of the offence by neglecting to exercise due care".
GIVEN `the parent can be found` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied the parent did not conduce by neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine must be ordered against the parent` IF
    `the parent can be found` AND (NOT `satisfied the parent did not conduce by neglect`)

-- s 44(3): "Where a Youth Court thinks that a charge ... is proved, the Court may make an order on the parent or guardian ... for
-- the payment of damages or costs or requiring him or her to give security for the good behaviour of the child or young person,
-- without proceeding to record a finding of guilt". A FINE is not in that list.
DECLARE ParentOrder IS ONE OF
    `parent pays damages`
    `parent pays costs`
    `parent gives security for good behaviour`
    `parent pays a fine`

GIVEN `the parent order` IS A ParentOrder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order may be made without recording a finding of guilt` IF
    CONSIDER `the parent order`
    WHEN `parent pays a fine` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `49 -- powers of the Youth Court on proof of an offence`

-- s 49(1): "where a Youth Court is satisfied that an offence has been proved, or where the child or young person ... admits the
-- facts constituting the offence, the Court, in addition to any other powers ..., has power --
--   (a) to discharge the offender;
--   (b) to discharge the offender upon the offender entering into a bond to be of good behaviour ...;
--   (c) to commit the offender to the care of a relative or other fit person for a period to be specified by the Court;
--   (d) to order the offender's parent or guardian to execute a bond to exercise proper care and guardianship ...;
--   (e) to make a probation order requiring the offender to be under the supervision of a probation officer or a volunteer
--       probation officer for a period of not less than 6 months and not more than 3 years;
--   (f) to make an order ... requiring the offender to perform community service, not exceeding 240 hours in aggregate ...;
--   (g) to order the offender to be detained in a place of detention for a period not exceeding 6 months;
--   (h) to order the offender to be detained in a place of detention or an approved institution over such number of weekends,
--       not exceeding 26, as the Court thinks fit;
--   (i) to order the offender to be sent to a juvenile rehabilitation centre for a period of not more than 3 years;
--   (j) to order the offender to pay a fine, damages or costs;
--   (k) to deal with the offender, or order the offender to be brought before a District Court to be dealt with, under section
--       305 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010" [reformative training] if, on the day of the finding of guilt, (A) the offender
--       has attained 18; or (B) is 14 to 17, was previously dealt with for another offence and was sent to a juvenile
--       rehabilitation centre under (i); or (C) is 14 to 17 and in the Court's opinion "of so unruly a character that the
--       offender cannot be safely detained in a juvenile rehabilitation centre or a place of detention"; and (ii) the Court is
--       satisfied the offender "should undergo a period of training in a reformative training centre".
-- s 46(1): "The words 'conviction' and 'sentence' cease to be used in relation to children and young persons dealt with by a
-- Youth Court."
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `discharge`
    `discharge on a good-behaviour bond`
    `committal to a relative or fit person`
    `parent's bond for proper care`
    `probation order`
    `community service order`
    `detention in a place of detention`
    `weekend detention`
    `juvenile rehabilitation centre`
    `fine, damages or costs`
    `reformative training`

DECLARE Offender HAS
    `age on the day of the finding` IS A NUMBER
    `previously sent to a juvenile rehabilitation centre` IS A BOOLEAN
    `too unruly for a JRC or place of detention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `court satisfied reformative training is needed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reformative training is available` IF
        `the offender`'s `court satisfied reformative training is needed`
    AND (    `the offender`'s `age on the day of the finding` AT LEAST 18
         OR  (    `the offender`'s `age on the day of the finding` AT LEAST 14
              AND `the offender`'s `age on the day of the finding` LESS THAN 18
              AND (`the offender`'s `previously sent to a juvenile rehabilitation centre` OR `the offender`'s `too unruly for a JRC or place of detention`)))

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is available on proof of the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `reformative training` THEN `reformative training is available` `the offender`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The limits in (e), (f), (g), (h) and (i). s 49(3): "Where the Youth Court makes an order under subsection (1)(g) ... in
-- combination with a probation order under subsection (1)(e), the period of the offender's detention must not exceed 3 months."
GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the probation period is within section 49(1)(e)` IF
    months AT LEAST 6 AND months AT MOST 36

GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the community service is within section 49(1)(f)` IF
    hours GREATER THAN 0 AND hours AT MOST 240

GIVEN `with probation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum detention in months under section 49(1)(g)` MEANS
    IF `with probation` THEN 3 ELSE 6

GIVEN weekends IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the weekend detention is within section 49(1)(h)` IF
    weekends GREATER THAN 0 AND weekends AT MOST 26

GIVEN months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the JRC period is within section 49(1)(i)` IF
    months GREATER THAN 0 AND months AT MOST 36

-- s 49(2)(a): the Court may make (b) to (j) singly, or combine "(i) any 2 or more of the orders referred to in subsection
-- (1)(b), (c), (d), (e), (f) and (j); (ii) any order under subsection (1)(g) with any one or more of the orders referred to in
-- subsection (1)(d), (e) and (j); (iii) any order under subsection (1)(h) with any one or more of the orders referred to in
-- subsection (1)(c), (d), (e), (f) and (j); or (iv) any order under subsection (1)(i) with any one or more of the orders referred
-- to in subsection (1)(d) and (j)"; (b): "without prejudice to paragraph (a)(ii) or (iii), to make an order under subsection
-- (1)(h) to run consecutively to an order under subsection (1)(g)". Discharge under (a) and reformative training under (k) are
-- not in any combination. The encoding tests PAIRS of different orders and treats (2)(b) as allowing (g) with (h).
GIVEN o IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the first combination group` IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `discharge on a good-behaviour bond` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `committal to a relative or fit person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `parent's bond for proper care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `probation order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `community service order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fine, damages or costs` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN o IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may go with detention` IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `parent's bond for proper care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `probation order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fine, damages or costs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `weekend detention` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN o IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may go with weekend detention` IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `committal to a relative or fit person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `parent's bond for proper care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `probation order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `community service order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fine, damages or costs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `detention in a place of detention` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN o IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may go with a JRC order` IF
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `parent's bond for proper care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fine, damages or costs` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN a IS AN Order, b IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pair may be combined one way` IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `detention in a place of detention` THEN `may go with detention` b
    WHEN `weekend detention` THEN `may go with weekend detention` b
    WHEN `juvenile rehabilitation centre` THEN `may go with a JRC order` b
    OTHERWISE (`is in the first combination group` a AND `is in the first combination group` b)

GIVEN a IS AN Order, b IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the two orders may be combined under section 49(2)` IF
    `the pair may be combined one way` a b OR `the pair may be combined one way` b a
